          <span class="section-label">Design Considerations</span>
          <h2>Indoor Court Design Factors</h2>
          <p>Indoor courts require special attention to environmental factors that don't affect outdoor courts. Our design process addresses these considerations from the start.</p>
          
          <h3>Critical Factors:</h3>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Ventilation:</strong> Proper air circulation prevents moisture buildup and ensures player comfort</li>
            <li><strong>Lighting:</strong> Uniform, glare-free lighting designed for sports visibility</li>
            <li><strong>Acoustics:</strong> Sound control to minimize noise transmission to other areas</li>
            <li><strong>Flooring:</strong> Appropriate surface systems for indoor conditions</li>
            <li><strong>Ceiling Height:</strong> Adequate clearance for ball trajectory and safety</li>
            <li><strong>Wall Protection:</strong> Impact-resistant wall systems and safety padding</li>
          </ul>
          
          <div class="tip-callout">
            <h4>Pro Tip</h4>
            <p>Consider installing retractable nets for multi-use spaces, allowing the area to serve multiple purposes when not used for sports.</p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

